---
import Base from '../layouts/base.astro'
---

<!--
  The commands in the <pre data-commands> blocks are what .github/workflows/selfhost.yml runs, read from this file by
  apps/site/scripts/page-commands.ts: change one here and the workflow runs the change. Write no braces and no opening angle
  bracket inside a block (Astro reads them).
-->
<Base
  title="Self-hosting"
  description="Run Free Planning Poker on your own machine with one compose file: the published image and PostgreSQL, started with a few commands."
>
  <h1>Self-hosting</h1>
  <p>
    Free Planning Poker is open source (AGPLv3). The room, the API and the database run from one compose file: the
    published image of the app and a PostgreSQL 18 container with a volume for its data. A workflow follows this page on
    a clean machine every night, so the commands below are the ones that work.
  </p>

  <h2 id="needs">What you need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Docker with Compose v2, the <code>docker compose</code> command, on Linux with an amd64 processor.</li>
    <li><code>curl</code> and <code>openssl</code> for the commands below; about 1 GB of memory for the two containers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="start">Start</h2>
  <p>
    The commands fetch the compose file and the example settings, write two generated secrets into <code>.env</code>
    and start both containers. They wait until both are healthy.
  </p>
  <pre data-commands="start"><code>mkdir free-planning-poker
cd free-planning-poker
curl -fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jkrumm/free-planning-poker/master/deploy/compose.yml
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jkrumm/free-planning-poker/master/deploy/.env.example -o .env
sed -i.bak "s|^POSTGRES_PASSWORD=.*|POSTGRES_PASSWORD=$(openssl rand -hex 24)|; s|^VISITOR_KEY=.*|VISITOR_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)|" .env
rm .env.bak
docker compose up -d --wait</code></pre>
  <p>
    Then open <a href="http://localhost:7740/room">http://localhost:7740/room</a>, create a room and share its link.
    Rooms live in the Docker volume <code>free-planning-poker_postgres-data</code>, so they survive a restart of the
    machine.
  </p>
  <p>
    Without the two secrets <code>docker compose up</code> stops and names the one that is missing. Every other setting
    has a default; <code>.env.example</code> lists each one with what happens when it is unset.
    The files are in the repository's
    <a href="https://github.com/jkrumm/free-planning-poker/tree/master/deploy">deploy folder</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="domain">Your own domain</h2>
  <p>
    The port is published on this machine only. To reach it from other machines, put a reverse proxy in front of it, or
    set <code>FPP_BIND=0.0.0.0</code> in <code>.env</code>. Then set <code>ALLOWED_ORIGINS</code> to the address people
    type, for example <code>https://poker.example.com</code>: the room refuses a browser whose origin is not listed.
    Behind a proxy that sets the client's address in a header, name the header in <code>CLIENT_IP_HEADER</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="update">Update</h2>
  <p>
    The image is <code>ghcr.io/jkrumm/free-planning-poker</code>. <code>latest</code> is the newest build of the main
    branch, <code>9.0.0</code> and the like are releases, and <code>sha-</code> followed by a commit's first seven
    characters is one commit. Set <code>FPP_IMAGE</code> in <code>.env</code> to stay on one of them. The database is
    migrated when the new container starts.
  </p>
  <pre data-commands="update"><code>docker compose pull
docker compose up -d --wait</code></pre>

  <h2 id="backup">Back up and restore</h2>
  <p>
    Back up with a dump of the database, not a copy of the volume: a copy taken while PostgreSQL runs may not be
    readable. The dump is one compressed file.
  </p>
  <pre data-commands="backup"><code>docker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U fpp --clean --if-exists fpp | gzip > fpp-backup.sql.gz</code></pre>
  <p>To restore it, stop the app, load the dump and start the app again.</p>
  <pre data-commands="restore"><code>docker compose stop api
gunzip -c fpp-backup.sql.gz | docker compose exec -T postgres psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -U fpp -d fpp
docker compose up -d --wait</code></pre>

  <h2 id="not-included">What is not included</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A TLS proxy.</strong> The app speaks plain HTTP. Put Caddy, nginx, Traefik or your cloud's load balancer
      in front of it, and keep WebSocket upgrades on.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics.</strong> The image sends nothing to Umami or any other analytics host, and none runs beside it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Telemetry.</strong> Off until you set <code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT</code> to your own OpenTelemetry
      collector, which you run yourself.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Mail for the contact form.</strong> The form answers that it is unavailable until you set a mail gateway
      in <code>.env</code>.
    </li>
    <li><strong>An image for arm64.</strong> The published image is for amd64 only.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
